# App Configuration Environment Variables
# Copy to .env and update as needed

# App to use (brighton, lincoln, etc.)
APP_ID=schoolzy

# Theme to use (defaults to app's themeId)
# THEME_ID=brighton

# ─── API Configuration ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL. Each app ships its own base URL in `apps/<variant>.ts` (Config.apiUrl),
# currently https://mobileappdev.schoolzyapp.com for all three.
# Set this only to point a build at a different environment — it overrides the
# per-app value. Expo inlines any EXPO_PUBLIC_* variable at build time, so
# changing it requires a rebuild, not just a reload.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://mobileappdev.schoolzyapp.com

# Value sent as the `api-version` query parameter on every /api/mobile/* call.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_VERSION=1.0

# ─── Feature flags ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTE: these are LOCAL / QA OVERRIDES only. The shipped values live in each
# app's `features` block in apps/<variant>.ts — that file is committed, so it is
# identical for every teammate and for CI. Release a change by editing it and
# running `eas update` (this .env is untracked; whoever runs the update would
# otherwise silently ship their own values).
# Dark mode is OFF: the app stays light even on a device set to dark.
# Set to 1 to follow the system colour scheme again. This drives both the JS
# theme and the native `userInterfaceStyle`, so it needs a rebuild — the dark
# palettes in apps/<variant>.ts are still there, nothing was deleted.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ENABLE_DARK_MODE=1

# Chat tab in the bottom navigation bar. OFF — the tab is hidden and
# ChattingScreen is never mounted. ChatWithSchool stays reachable as a root
# screen. Set to 1 to show the tab again.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ENABLE_CHAT_TAB=1

# Requests placement. ON — Requests is a bottom-bar tab and the row is removed
# from the Account screen. Set to 0 to hide the tab and move Requests back onto
# Account. The two placements are mutually exclusive.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ENABLE_REQUESTS_TAB=0

# Payment methods on the Payment Details screen — one flag each.
# Only InstaPay is ON: Apple Pay and the wallet have no payment-submission
# endpoint behind them yet, so they would show a success screen that never
# reached the server. Switch each on when its backend exists.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ENABLE_APPLE_PAY=1
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ENABLE_INSTAPAY=0
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ENABLE_WALLET=1

# ─── Debugging ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Logs are on automatically in development. Push notifications and Firebase only
# work in a real build (where __DEV__ is false), so set this to 1 to keep the
# request/response and push logs in preview/production builds.
# View them with: npx react-native log-android  |  npx react-native log-ios
# EXPO_PUBLIC_DEBUG_LOGS=1

# Build Configuration
# VERSION=1.0.0
# BUILD_NUMBER=1
